# Anchored to the repository root on purpose. Unanchored, `out/` matches at any depth, and this
# codebase puts outbound ports in packages named `port/out` — so the first outbound port written
# was ignored, staged nothing, and committed a build that only compiled because the file was
# still on disk. A web build directory belongs to whichever subproject produces it; when the
# editor arrives it can ignore its own.
/out/
/dist/
/.next/
/data/
